#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# q_gamma

#% text
# `q_gamma(z, q)` gives the q-gamma function `(q; q)_inf/(q^z; q)_inf*(1 - q)^(1 - z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 5.18.4, for `0 < q < 1`. It satisfies `q_gamma(z + 1, q) = (1 - q^z)/(1 - q)*q_gamma(z, q)` and `q_gamma(1, q) = 1`, and tends to `gamma(z)` as `q` tends to 1.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
q_gamma(1, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
q_gamma(3.0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1.5

#% cell
q_gamma(2.5, 0.9)
#% output
#= 1.303939613392059

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The recurrence:

#% cell
q_gamma(3.7, 0.6) - (1 - 0.6^2.7)/(1 - 0.6)*q_gamma(2.7, 0.6)
#% output
#= -4.440892098500626e-16

#% text
# As `q` grows towards 1 it approaches `gamma(2.5)` = 1.3293...:

#% cell
[q_gamma(2.5, 0.9), q_gamma(2.5, 0.99), gamma(2.5)]
#% output
#= [1.303939613392059, 1.3268432717873382, 1.329340388179137]

